.TH AENIGMA-TOR 8 "2026-08-10" "aenigma 5.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Scripts"
.SH NAME
aenigma-tor \- configure and publish a Tor hidden service for an
Aenigma application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-tor
.B \-l
.I LOCAL_ADDRESS
.B \-o
.I ONION_PORT
.B \-s
.I SERVICE_NAME
.RB [ \-u
.IR AUTHORIZED_USER ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR CONFIG_ADDRESS ]
.br
.B aenigma-tor
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-tor
installs and configures the Tor daemon, if not already present, and
publishes a local network service as a Tor hidden service (onion
service).
.PP
The script performs the following actions:
.IP \(bu 2
Installs the
.B tor
package via
.B apt
if the
.B tor
binary is not already present, then enables and starts the
.B tor
systemd service.
.IP \(bu 2
Creates the hidden service directory
.I /var/lib/tor/SERVICE_NAME
owned by the
.B debian-tor
user and group, with permissions restricted to
.B 700 ,
as required by Tor.
.IP \(bu 2
Appends a
.B HiddenServiceDir
/
.B HiddenServicePort
block to
.IR /etc/tor/torrc ,
optionally followed by a
.B HiddenServiceAuthorizeClient
.B stealth
line if
.B \-u
is given. If a block for the same
.I SERVICE_NAME
already exists in
.IR /etc/tor/torrc ,
the script does not modify it and no new block is appended; existing
Tor configuration for that service is left untouched.
.IP \(bu 2
Restarts Tor and waits (up to 120 seconds) for the hidden service
hostname file to be generated.
.IP \(bu 2
Prints the resulting
.I .onion
address, and, if requested via
.BR \-c ,
records it in the Aenigma application configuration.
.PP
.B aenigma-tor
must be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-l " LOCAL_ADDRESS"
The local address and port on which the target service is already
listening, e.g.
.IR 127.0.0.1:8080 .
This is used as the destination of the
.B HiddenServicePort
mapping in
.IR torrc .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-o " ONION_PORT"
The port on which the onion service should accept incoming
connections from Tor clients, e.g.
.IR 80 .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-s " SERVICE_NAME"
Name used to identify the onion service. Determines the hidden
service directory,
.IR /var/lib/tor/SERVICE_NAME .
Required.
.TP
.BI \-u " AUTHORIZED_USER"
Enables Tor client authorization (stealth mode) for the onion
service and registers
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
via
.BR aenigma-tor-auth (8).
Adds a
.B "HiddenServiceAuthorizeClient stealth"
line to the generated
.I torrc
block. Optional.
.TP
.BI \-c " CONFIG_ADDRESS"
If set to
.IR 1 ,
the resulting onion address is recorded in the Aenigma application
configuration by invoking
.BR aenigma-config (8)
with the
.B OnionService
property. If set to
.I 0
or omitted, the configuration step is skipped. Optional.
.TP
.B \-h
Display a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The onion service was configured successfully and its address was
printed.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid or missing arguments, the script was not run as root, or the
onion service hostname file was not generated within the timeout
period.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tor/torrc
Tor daemon configuration file; appended to by this script.
.TP
.I /var/lib/tor/SERVICE_NAME
Hidden service data directory, owned by
.BR debian-tor .
.TP
.I /var/lib/tor/SERVICE_NAME/hostname
Generated by Tor; contains the published
.I .onion
address.
.SH EXAMPLES
Publish a local web application on port 8080 as an onion service on
port 80:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo aenigma-tor \-l 127.0.0.1:8080 \-o 80 \-s aenigma-dashboard
.EE
.RE
.PP
Publish the same service with Tor client authorization for user
.IR admin ,
and record the resulting address in the Aenigma configuration:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo aenigma-tor \-l 127.0.0.1:8080 \-o 80 \-s aenigma-dashboard \e
    \-u admin \-c 1
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
Re-running
.B aenigma-tor
for a
.I SERVICE_NAME
that already has a matching
.B HiddenServiceDir
entry in
.I torrc
has no effect on the existing entry; the script will not update the
port, local address, or authorization settings of an already
configured service. To change these values, edit
.I /etc/tor/torrc
manually and restart Tor.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tor (8),
.BR aenigma-proxy (8),
.BR aenigma-config (8),
.BR aenigma-tor-auth (8),
.BR torrc (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.ruja@aenigma.ro>
